			"id": "agent-analysis-hmosword-build-sample-onboarding",
			"interpretation": "Responsibility: hmosword-build is a Node.js bootstrap helper that clones external HarmonyOS_Samples repos per config/mock.json into ../submodules/ and rewrites each so it registers as a feature module in build-profile.json5. Scope: hmosword-build/{index.js, package.json, config/mock.json} + image/* + screenshots/* PNG (json5 ^2.2.3 is package.json's only dep); writes touch parent build-profile.json5, ../submodules/<sampleName>/, each clone's module.json5/oh-package.json5/build-profile.json5. Behavior: index.js needs fs/path/child_process + json5; readMock iterates mock.json.data; per item derives sampleName + samplePath, skips clone if non-empty, else async `git clone -b <branch> <originalUrl> <samplePath>`; processSample/processSampleWithoutConfig then rewrite the clone (entry->moduleName rename, oh-package.json5.name rewrite, src/main/module.json5 -> type='feature'/deliveryWithInstall=false/abilities[0].name=abilityName/exported=false); configured samples map clone build-profile.json5 modules entry->feature/others leaf; writeBuildProfile appends new modules to parent build-profile.json5.modules; only entry-derived entries carry default-product targets.",
			"kind": "analysis",
			"limitations": ["Whether `git clone -b <branch>` succeeds for every originalUrl/branch pair in config/mock.json is unverified: network reachability, SSH/auth availability, and rename drift in the upstream HarmonyOS_Samples repos are not provable from this checkout.","Whether the rewritten modules actually compile under hvigor is unverified; processSampleWithoutConfig only mutates modules whose existing type is 'entry', and silently skips samples whose ohosTest-only module.json5 tree yields an empty cloneSamples list.","The substringFromStartToEnd(moduleName, 6) naming convention assumes every configured moduleName is exactly 6 characters longer than the desired directory name; off-by-one or character-set edge cases are not exercised here.","deleteExtraDir is invoked with (samplePath, needModules) but its declared third parameter moduleName is never used; the cleanup semantics for samples whose build-profile.json5 is missing or whose needModules list is empty are not validated by the source alone."],
